Let me second this; there is no question that if I were not making the
effort to run a public server and support the idea of a subcommunity of
Nethack players, I would not be enjoying what success I have had.

The assumption that Nethack is played primarily by people who are willing 
and capable to compile it themselves is no longer true, and may not have
been true for quite some time.  With distributed binaries and packages
available for many *nices, as well as the ubiquitous Windows precompiled
setups, the target audience has definitely changed a great deal,
certainly where new players are concerned.

Some of L's patches should have received a much wider audience than they 
did, for example, but I suspect less than twenty people ever played them --
because it was necessary to compile your own personal binary to do so.

